testing/goldens — one committed cell grid per chrome surface

WHAT THESE ARE

Each file is `ktui_draw_dump()`'s output for one front end at one size: the
libktui cell buffer as plain text, every row padded to the full width, one
line per row. `testing/selftest.sh` renders the same frame and diffs.

WHY, beyond the shape checks that were already there

selftest.sh already asserted that a dump is SQUARE — every row the same width,
enough rows to be a box. S1 (the double-buffer stale-row bug: paint diffed
against libktui's single global front buffer while every commit alternated
buffers, so the other buffer's rows went stale) passed that check on every
frame it corrupted. Every row was the right width and every row was wrong.
A golden is the only check that notices.

HOW TO REGENERATE

    KDOS_GOLDEN_UPDATE=1 testing/selftest.sh

then read the diff in `git diff testing/goldens/` before committing it. That
diff IS the review: it is a picture of what the change did to the screen.

THE RULE FOR ADDING ONE

A golden is committed only for a dump that is deterministic on ANY host — no
clock, no hostname, no readdir order, no absolute paths, nothing read out of
the developer's own /usr/share. Everything the surface reads comes from
`testing/fixtures/shell/` (`tree/` for the file chooser, `config/` for the
surfaces that parse an rc.xml or a comp.conf), frozen there on purpose so a
golden cannot move because somebody edited skel.

A surface that cannot meet that is left out and SAID SO in selftest.sh's
comment beside the list — cal draws the current month, the launcher scans the
host's /usr/share/applications, kdos-saver seeds from time() ^ getpid(),
kdos-slit renders the output of forked commands, the panel needs a live
compositor. A golden pinned with a hack nobody can reproduce is worse than a
missing one.

Most dumps are ASCII: `ktui_caps` is 0 with no terminal, so a surface drawing
straight to a buffer gets the ascii tier. `con-view-80x24.txt` is the exception
and is not ASCII — it comes through a real view process, which reports UTF-8
and is given the rich tier. A dump's tier follows whoever painted it, not the
fact that it is a dump. The rich and vt tiers are covered by the ramp
assertions in `src/libs/selftest.c`.

WHAT IS STILL MISSING

`--dump-cells` — one line per non-blank cell, `row col U+XXXX fg bg attr` —
is the other half of the contract and no surface implements it yet. It is what
would make a COLOUR regression visible as well as a geometry one, and it is
what `kdos chrome --audit` (D7) is meant to be built on. selftest.sh probes for
it and says out loud that it is not there.
